    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0351" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1932v02/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5131/931a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France
                        (Edge)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-12-23T18:00:00-05:00">December 23, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>451. At press conference today a correspondent made inquiry as to the status of
                    the commercial treaty. I stated in reply “The negotiations <pb facs="0352"
                        n="262" xml:id="pg262"/> have not been broken off, but in view of the
                    urgency of satisfactorily disposing of more important matters, the actual
                    negotiations are for the present being held in abeyance”.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
